From 428b7bb211eb86b1e881cb698db290956345292a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Instrument the word lookup end to end and harden the popup
 rows

The dictionary senses still did not show on the device even though
the parse layer was believed correct - which is exactly the problem:
believing instead of knowing. The dictionary classes were now run
locally against the live APIs (outside Android, with the same
okhttp/org.json stack), and they do produce full entries: apple
returns its sense, business its sense plus the IELTS and business
labels the user saw, and the Microsoft translator returns plain
translations. The code is correct; what differs on the device can
only be the network path or the rendering, and guessing between them
has already cost two rounds.

So the whole pipeline now logs into the Bisub debug log: the request
URL, the HTTP status with size and duration, the parsed field
counts, every parsed sense, the popup's headline/secondary colors as
hex values, and how many rows fill() added. One logcat read will now
pinpoint the layer that breaks on the device.

While at it, the row colors are taken from getCurrentTextColor() -
the color the headline is actually drawn with, so visible headline
guarantees visible rows - and the rows carry explicit
LinearLayout.LayoutParams. The dark popup also gets its requested
makeover: 85% translucency (up from 94%) and a real backdrop blur -
frosted glass - on Android 12 and above, where the system allows
cross-window blur; older devices keep the plain translucency.
